  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Some players, by choice or otherwise, can only use the Chatbox text to communicate.  However it is easy to miss when someone says speaks this way (an audio signal would be handy, as another suggestion points out), but it would be great if there was a way to maintain some kind of chatbox history.  Couldn't you add the ability to create a chatbox window that you can grab and move anywhere on your display, which can contain the chatbox history of players in world?  It wouldn't be different from an Instant Messenger window, after all.\n\nGood features of course would be to toggle whether this UI window is visible or not, toggle to minimize/restore it instead of making it go completely away, and some way to organize multiple chatbox histories.\n\nI'd say the contents of the window should be cleared whenever you go to a new world (since the game doesn't have the concept of IM'ing players on different worlds, which would be a nice ability, I mean you can do it with Second Life).\n\nBut this would be helpful to not miss something someone said via chatbox, but to maintain a history that you could go back to.",
